Saturday evening, Ludwig is lying asleep next to me on the sofa.
He is very tired after our walk in the forest.
I open my computer and video call home to my family in Mexico.
My sister Sofía and my brother Diego are sitting ready in front of the screen.
"You simply must see my little guest," I say to them.
I take the computer and point the camera down at the dog.
Sofía smiles happily.
"Just look at him!"
"He sure is cute," Diego says.
Ludwig opens one eye, but he just stays lying down.
"Look at him."
"He is just as calm as our dog Lola back home," I say.
Diego asks me if he is an easy dog to look after.
"Yes, I really like looking after him," I answer.
"He just has to walk on a leash out on the street."
"And he definitely must not have human food."
"So I only give him his own treats."
Suddenly we hear Lola bark loudly in the background on the video.
Ludwig lifts his head and looks very confused at the screen.
"Just lie down again, my friend," I say gently and pet him.
I say goodnight to my family so he can get some peace.
He closes his eyes and quickly falls back asleep.
